      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Creating a comprehensive verbal de-escalation protocol is a crucial initiative for your new ED team in Chicago, especially given the recent rise in agitation. The process typically begins with ensuring your own safety while approaching the patient calmly and establishing rapport using clear, non-threatening language. Key steps include maintaining an open body language, actively listening to the patient's concerns, and offering limited but specific choices to foster a sense of control. Finally, if verbal techniques fail to calm the patient and physical restraint becomes unavoidable, ensure you have clear institutional policies and legal standards in place to guide the next steps.",
